## Chat-switching signals — when to suggest pausing the chat

Proactively tell Banana when a chat should end. Use these signals:

| Signal | What to say |
|---|---|
| **Cluster merged successfully** | "This cluster is complete and merged. Strongly recommend closing this chat and starting a fresh one for the next iteration. Here's the handoff block to paste in the next chat:" + [HANDOFF BLOCK] |
| **Cluster rolled back** | "This cluster was rolled back. Fresh chat strongly recommended for the next attempt — the context here will bias the next fix toward the same approach that failed. Here's the handoff:" + [HANDOFF BLOCK] |
| **Chat exceeds 30 turns and cluster isn't close to done** | "This chat is getting long. Performance can degrade past this length. Suggest pausing and continuing in a fresh chat with the following handoff:" + [HANDOFF BLOCK] |
| **Scope shifted to a different cluster** | "What you're asking is in a different cluster than the one this session started on. Recommend capturing handoff and starting a new chat for that cluster. Here's the handoff:" + [HANDOFF BLOCK] |
| **Banana context-switched (next day, after long pause)** | "Welcome back. Before continuing, suggest a fresh chat so context loads cleanly. Here's the handoff to paste:" + [HANDOFF BLOCK] |

Suggest, don't force. Banana decides whether to switch. But always include the handoff block when you suggest — make it trivially easy for her to accept.

---

## The handoff block — standardized format

When suggesting a chat switch, produce this block exactly. It's what Banana copies into the next chat:

```
═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
HANDOFF FOR NEXT CHAT
═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════

JUST COMPLETED: <iteration-tag>
- Branch: <feat-branch-name>
- Status: <Merged to main | Merged to staging | Rolled back | In progress>
- One-line summary: <what changed>

KICKOFF FOR NEXT CHAT — paste this verbatim:
─────────────────────────────────────────────
You are picking up BBB (Bertrand the Banana Butler) work in this repo.

Follow the BBB session protocol in @.cursor/rules/bbb-session-protocol.mdc.

Current state: @_docs/planning/QA/BBB-ITERATION-LOG.csv
Spec for this iteration: @<NEXT-SPEC-FILE-PATH>
This session's work: implement <NEXT-ITERATION-TAG> per the spec above.
Read the spec in full before producing the plan — do not skim.

Continuing from <PREVIOUS-ITERATION-TAG> which just merged. Watch for
regressions in: <SPECIFIC AREAS the prior cluster might affect>.

Start by reading the iteration log row for this iteration, then the spec
file. Then give me a 5-line plan of what you will change and in what
order. Wait for my approval before touching code.
─────────────────────────────────────────────

DECIDE LATER — items raised but out of scope:
- <item 1, if any>
- <item 2, if any>

CSV ROW UPDATE — update these fields in Airtable for this iteration:
─────────────────────────────────────────────
iteration_tag: <tag>
status: <Done | Rolled Back | Paused | etc.>
merge_date: YYYY-MM-DD (if merged)
description: <update to add what actually shipped, if needed>
watch: <update if new risk flags surfaced>
notes: <any new notes — Cursor session findings, decide-later items>
─────────────────────────────────────────────

═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
```

Fill in every field. Don't skip "DECIDE LATER" — if there's nothing, write `none`. The "CSV ROW UPDATE" section gives Banana the exact field=value pairs to update in Airtable for the iteration_tag row.

